    "collateral_ratio_scale": "percent",
    "collateral_ratio_basis": "Issuer-attested collateralization, published unchanged. NETTED ON BOTH SIDES: (reserves - POL - inventory) / (supply - POL - inventory), the basis apyx switched to on 2026-06-08. POL is protocol-owned liquidity and Inventory is a net-zero bucket, so both are removed from backing and from supply rather than counted as either. \u26a0\ufe0f NOT comparable to a gross collateral ratio: the generic axis cutoffs assume gross, so a netted figure sits lower for the same underlying coverage. We verify the identity independently \u2014 residual tolerance 0.01pp \u2014 rather than trusting the attested number on its own; see asset_specific.backing_attestation.attested_basis_residual_pp. \u26a0\ufe0f Netting makes this asset look WORSE, not better: gross is 99.20% against the netted 98.86%, -0.34pp. Do not read a netted basis as issuer-flattering.",
    "axis_rating_basis": "Rated on the generic band deliberately \u2014 no anchor exists in this analyzer, and the apparent agreement between the axis (2/5) and the published backing score (2.0/10) is COINCIDENTAL. The axis rates coverage; the score rates basket composition (~74% STRC) and dislocation, which a collateral ratio cannot express. Expect them to diverge when STRC moves without the CR moving \u2014 that is the design, not a defect.",
